Hi,

Please look at my PR, which introduces setting editor.insertSpaceAfterComment to make VScode to format line comments like

```
		//model.tokenizeIfCheap(startLineNumber);
```
instead of 
```
		// model.tokenizeIfCheap(startLineNumber);
```
(no space just after //)

By default original behaviour is remained, with the space.

We set the file size limit to 300MB (on 32bit) and 16GB (on 64bit) based memory optimization and analysis in https://github.com/Microsoft/vscode/issues/30180 . As described in https://github.com/Microsoft/vscode/issues/42839, v8 heap size limit is making this limit smaller on 64bit. In this PR, we check `max_old_space_size` first and if it's exceeding v8's limit, we show error message to users and ask them to run `code --max_old_space_size={LARGERSIZE}` to workaround.

@alexandrudima Can we remove the general file size limit, as we are moving to the new buffer and v8 is the limit ?

cc @bpasero

